+less 710 - Windows ARM64 baseline benchmark (base_bench_win_arm)
+===================================================================
+Upstream less has no benchmark suite; this uses benchmarks/run_bench.sh
+(added in this commit). Lower is better. Times are wall-clock ms for one
+full less process run (startup + work + exit), 1 warm-up + 7 timed runs.
+
+Host   : Snapdragon(R) X Elite - X1E80100 - Qualcomm(R) Oryon(TM) CPU, Windows 11 build 26100, native ARM64
+Input  : 1,000,000 generated lines (~62 MB) + final line "ZZEND marker 424242"
+         (generated by run_bench.sh with awk; deterministic)
+Env    : TERM=xterm LINES=40 COLUMNS=120, LESS/LESSOPEN unset
+
+Builds:
+  arm64-msys : C:\wos-eval\work\less\less.exe + less_t.exe (aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc 17.0.0, -g -O2,
+               PCRE2, ARM64 msys-2.0.dll 3.6.10 from C:\msys64\usr\aarch64-pc-cygwin\usr\bin)
+               run from a pure ARM64 process tree (ARM64 bash from the sysroot)
+  arm64-msvc : C:\wos-eval\work\less-msvc-build\less.exe (MSVC 14.51 ARM64, Makefile.wnm);
+               pipe_cat only (no LESSTEST hooks), BENCH_WINPATH=1
+  x64-msys   : C:\wos-eval\work\less-x64-build\less.exe + less_t.exe (x86_64 gcc 16.2.0, -g -O2,
+               PCRE2, x64 msys-2.0.dll 3.6.12) run under x64 emulation (Prism) from the x64 MSYS shell
+
+Cases:
+  pipe_cat     less FILE > file            non-tty copy path (output cmp'd vs input: identical)
+  search_fwd   less_t --tty keys -n FILE   keys: /ZZEND m[a-z]+ [0-9]{6}$ <CR> q  (PCRE2, scan to EOF)
+  search_back  less_t --tty keys -n FILE   keys: G ?^line 1: <CR> q             (backward scan from EOF)
+  linenum_end  less_t --tty keys -N FILE   keys: G q                             (line numbering to EOF)
+  (less_t = same sources/flags as less.exe plus -DLESSTEST, which adds --tty so keystrokes can be
+   scripted without a pty, exactly as upstream lesstest drives it)
+
+Commands:
+  ARM64 (from cmd.exe, pure ARM64 tree):
+    C:\msys64\usr\aarch64-pc-cygwin\usr\bin\bash.exe -c 'export PATH=/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin:/usr/bin; cd /c/wos-eval/work;
+      sh less/benchmarks/run_bench.sh arm64-msys /c/wos-eval/work/less/less.exe /c/wos-eval/work/less/less_t.exe /c/wos-eval/work/less-bench-data 7;
+      BENCH_WINPATH=1 sh less/benchmarks/run_bench.sh arm64-msvc /c/wos-eval/work/less-msvc-build/less.exe "" /c/wos-eval/work/less-bench-data 7'
+  x64 (emulated):
+    MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /c/wos-eval/work; sh less/benchmarks/run_bench.sh x64-msys
+      /c/wos-eval/work/less-x64-build/less.exe /c/wos-eval/work/less-x64-build/less_t.exe /c/wos-eval/work/less-bench-data 7'
+
+Raw results:
+arm64-msys   pipe_cat     min=   472 ms  median=   528 ms  mean=   528.3 ms  n=7  rc=0
+arm64-msys   search_fwd   min=  1197 ms  median=  1222 ms  mean=  1215.1 ms  n=7  rc=0
+arm64-msys   search_back  min=  1441 ms  median=  1452 ms  mean=  1453.1 ms  n=7  rc=0
+arm64-msys   linenum_end  min=   297 ms  median=   300 ms  mean=   300.3 ms  n=7  rc=0
+arm64-msvc   pipe_cat     min=   577 ms  median=   603 ms  mean=   596.6 ms  n=7  rc=0
+x64-msys     pipe_cat     min=   877 ms  median=   901 ms  mean=   901.4 ms  n=7  rc=0
+x64-msys     search_fwd   min=  1821 ms  median=  1864 ms  mean=  1863.3 ms  n=7  rc=0
+x64-msys     search_back  min=  1820 ms  median=  1840 ms  mean=  1849.6 ms  n=7  rc=0
+x64-msys     linenum_end  min=   555 ms  median=   568 ms  mean=   567.0 ms  n=7  rc=0
+
+Summary (median ms; speedup = x64-emulated / arm64-native):
+  case          arm64-msys   x64-msys(emu)   speedup   arm64-msvc
+  pipe_cat          528          901          1.71x        603
+  search_fwd       1222         1864          1.53x         -
+  search_back      1452         1840          1.27x         -
+  linenum_end       300          568          1.89x         -
+
+Notes:
+  - pipe_cat was noisier on ARM64 in this run (an earlier run of the same binary with
+    output to /dev/null gave median 377 ms vs 784 ms for x64); numbers are recorded as-is.
+  - MSVC less is not run with stdout=/dev/null: the MSVC CRT reports NUL as a tty and less
+    then waits for keyboard input.
